{
  "case": "release notes from merged PRs",
  "variant": "without",
  "trial": 4,
  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 entry to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, in the same format as the earlier entries:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * BREAKING: Remove deprecated --legacy flag from sync (ACME-421)\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\nThe version and date come from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files. All five PRs from `merged_prs.txt` are included, with the breaking change listed first.\n\n**Decision for you:** ACME-421 is marked as breaking (the `!`), but the release is numbered 2.4.0. Under semantic versioning, a removed flag would normally mean a major bump to 3.0.0. Anyone running `sync --legacy` in scripts will see it fail after what looks like a routine upgrade. I kept 2.4.0 because it's what `VERSION` says. If you want 3.0.0, update `VERSION` and I'll change the heading to match.",
